[4792]={"'If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at building, upgrading, and firing siege equipment</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.\
\
'Engineers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>build siege equipment and other devices more quickly</b></rgb>. They also have more options for <rgb=#FFFF00><b>upgrading and repairing</b></rgb> such devices, and can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>place traps</b></rgb> to hinder the enemy.\
\
'Engineers can also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>disable enemy traps</b></rgb>.'","'Selecting the Commander will highlight all of the soldiers under his command.\
\
'During battle, by <rgb=#FFFF00><b>speaking with someone 'Awaiting Orders,' like a Commander,</b></rgb> you can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change the tactics of a group of soldiers</b></rgb>. \
\
'Some options are available at the outset, such as <rgb=#FFFF00><b>healing the soldiers</b></rgb> over time and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>increasing their damage output</b></rgb>.\
\
'Other options become available  <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.'","'Saruman's armies will soon be here, ${PLAYER}, but I fear that my companions do not know what to expect. <rgb=#FFFF00><b>An Epic Battle is not like the engagements we have faced to this point</b></rgb>, and I want to ensure that our friends are ready.\
\
'I would count mere survival of the battle a success, given the foes arrayed before us, but <rgb=#FFFF00><b>the truest victory is one in which we overcome all the challenges</b></rgb> the battle brings. As a battle ebbs and flows, we may be presented with <rgb=#FFFF00><b>optional secondary objectives</b></rgb>. These are <rgb=#FFFF00><b>not necessary for victory, but completing them successfully will add to the Merit we earn</b></rgb> in the battle: the measure of our victory.'","Talk to the Engineer and learn about Siege Equipment","'We have fought large numbers of enemies before, but never so many foes as this! There will <rgb=#FFFF00><b>simply be too many enemies</b></rgb> for one hero to dispatch alone. We must <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use other methods</b></rgb> against them if we are to survive.'","'<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Enemies will march in formations</b></rgb> toward us. When a formation reaches our position, enemies will engage in close combat. We should <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use siege equipment to lessen their numbers first</b></rgb>, before that happens!\
\
'<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Anyone can build and use basic siege equipment</b></rgb>.\
\
'Other options become available <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.\
\
'If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at building, upgrading, and firing siege equipment</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.\
\
'Engineers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>build siege equipment and other devices more quickly</b></rgb>. They also have more options for <rgb=#FFFF00><b>upgrading and repairing</b></rgb> such devices, and can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>place traps</b></rgb> to hinder the enemy.\
\
'Engineers can also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>disable enemy traps</b></rgb>.'","'If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at issuing orders to Commanders</b></rgb> and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>provide useful buffs to your allies</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.\
\
'Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>issue more effective orders to Commanders</b></rgb>. They also have more commands at their disposal, and can make a group of soldiers <rgb=#FFFF00><b>focus on particular targets</b></rgb> or <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change their weapons</b></rgb>.\
\
Officers can command soldiers to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>shelter from incoming catapult shells or arrows</b></rgb>.\
\
'Additionally, Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>plant banners that aid nearby Engineers and Vanguards</b></rgb>.'","Talk to Aragorn and learn about Epic Battles","Talk to the Engineer and learn about the Engineer Role","'If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>stand toe-to-toe with enemy forces</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Vanguard Battle Role</b></rgb>.\
\
'Vanguards <rgb=#FFFF00><b>unlock powerful attacks by earning Killstreaks</b></rgb>, defeating many enemies in succession. They also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>receive benefits by dealing and receiving damage</b></rgb>, and can also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>run faster</b></rgb> than other heroes.\
\
'A Vanguard is happiest when <rgb=#FFFF00><b>engaging in close-quarters combat</b></rgb>.'","Aragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.","'We have fought large numbers of enemies before, but never so many foes as this! There will <rgb=#FFFF00><b>simply be too many enemies</b></rgb> for one hero to dispatch alone.\
\
'We must <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use other methods</b></rgb> against them if we are to survive.'","'Saruman's armies will soon be here, ${PLAYER}, but I fear that my companions do not know what to expect. <rgb=#FFFF00><b>An Epic Battle is not like the engagements we have faced to this point</b></rgb>, and I want to ensure that our friends are ready.'","Talk to Aragorn and learn about Merit","Talk to Aragorn and learn about Battle Roles","Listen to Aragorn and his companions discuss the coming battle","'<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Enemies will march in formations</b></rgb> towards us. When a formation reaches our position, enemies will engage in close combat. We should <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use siege equipment to lessen their numbers first</b></rgb>, before that happens!\
\
'<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Anyone can build and use basic siege equipment</b></rgb>.\
\
'Other options become available <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.'","Talk to the Officer and learn about Commanders","Talk to the Officer and learn about the Officer Role","'It is very complicated, but I believe I understand what Aragorn has said to us. We will do well, ${PLAYER}, I am certain of it!'","Listen to Aragorn and his companions discuss Merit and medals","'I believe I know enough for now, ${PLAYER}. I hope you feel the same! This land will not give in to Saruman's designs without a fight!'","'I would count mere survival of the battle a success, given the foes arrayed before us, but <rgb=#FFFF00><b>the truest victory is one in which we overcome all the challenges</b></rgb> the battle brings.\
\
'As a battle ebbs and flows, we may be presented with <rgb=#FFFF00><b>optional side objectives</b></rgb>.\
\
'These are <rgb=#FFFF00><b>not necessary for victory, but completing them successfully will add to the Merit we earn</b></rgb> in the battle: the measure of our victory.'","The armies of Saruman approach the Hornburg, and Aragorn wishes to help his companions prepare for the epic battle soon to be joined.","'There are three different Battle Roles in which you can specialize, ${PLAYER}. These Roles are <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Engineer</b></rgb>, <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Vanguard</b></rgb>, and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Officer</b></rgb>.\
\
'By performing well during battle, you will <rgb=#FFFF00><b>earn points you can spend on these Roles in the Promotions Panel</b></rgb>, becoming more effective at your chosen specialization.\
\
'Speak with each of the representatives here to learn what each Battle Role has to offer.'","Talk to the Vanguard and learn about the Vanguard Role","'Selecting the Commander will highlight all of the soldiers under his command.\
\
'During battle, by <rgb=#FFFF00><b>speaking with someone 'Awaiting Orders,' like a Commander,</b></rgb> you can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change the tactics of a group of soldiers</b></rgb>. \
\
'Some options are available at the outset, such as <rgb=#FFFF00><b>healing the soldiers</b></rgb> over time and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>increasing their damage output</b></rgb>.\
\
'Other options become available  <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.\
\
'If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at issuing orders to Commanders</b></rgb> and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>provide useful buffs to your allies</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.\
\
'Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>issue more effective orders to Commanders</b></rgb>. They have more commands at their disposal, and can make a group of soldiers <rgb=#FFFF00><b>focus on particular targets</b></rgb> or <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change their weapons</b></rgb>.\
\
'Officers can also command soldiers to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>shelter from incoming catapult shells or arrows</b></rgb>.\
\
'Additionally, Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>plant banners that aid nearby Engineers and Vanguards</b></rgb>.'","Talk to Gimli when you are done learning about Epic Battles for now","Talk to Legolas and learn about Approaching Enemies","Listen to Legolas and his companions discuss the effectiveness of dealing with enemies at range","Batallas Épicas: Entrenamiento Básico"},
[4802]={"El gremio de cocineros de Umbar Baharbêl suministra alimentos a las tabernas, a la Hermandad y a todo el mundo. Necesitan ayuda para satisfacer las demandas de la gente.","Entrega una caja de comida al líder del Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar.","La receta necesaria para completar esta misión está disponible para su compra. <rgb=#00f000>Compra la receta de la misión al líder del gremio.</rgb>\
\
Crea una caja de comida cocinada para Umbar Baharbêl.","'Excelente. Esta comida satisfará las necesidades de los posaderos de los barrios bajos.'","'Buen día. Me complace que te hayas unido a nuestro gremio. Agradezco que estés dispuesto a ayudarnos a satisfacer las demandas impuestas al gremio. La comida es un lazo que une a los más humildes y a los más ricos, y nosotros satisfacemos las peticiones de todos.\
\
'Como miembro, contamos contigo para que nos ayudes a satisfacer las peticiones de la siempre exigente población. ¿Estás preparado para cumplir con tu parte?'","Elabora una caja de comida cocinada para el Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar.","Demandas epicúreas (diario)","Entrega los platos cocinados al líder del Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar.","Elaborada una caja de comida cocinada para el Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar."},
[4803]={"El gremio de cocineros de Umbar Baharbêl suministra alimentos a las tabernas, a la Hermandad y a todo el mundo. Necesitan ayuda para satisfacer las demandas de la gente.","Entrega una caja de comida al líder del Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar.","La receta necesaria para completar esta misión está disponible para su compra. <rgb=#00f000>Compra la receta de la misión al líder del gremio.</rgb>\
\
Crea una caja de comida cocinada para Umbar Baharbêl.","'Excelente. Esta comida satisfará las necesidades de los posaderos de los barrios bajos.'","'Buen día. Me complace que te hayas unido a nuestro gremio. Agradezco que estés dispuesto a ayudarnos a satisfacer las demandas impuestas al gremio. La comida es un lazo que une a los más humildes y a los más ricos, y nosotros satisfacemos las peticiones de todos.\
\
'Como miembro, contamos contigo para que nos ayudes a satisfacer las peticiones de la siempre exigente población. ¿Estás preparado para cumplir con tu parte?'","Elabora una caja de comida cocinada para el Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar.","Demandas epicúreas (diario)","Entrega los platos cocinados al líder del Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar.","Elaborada una caja de comida cocinada para el Gremio de Cocineros de Umbar."},
[4805]={"Caebar waits for you in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.","'Give Caebar the papers my brother collected during our time in the Fearwater.'","Talk to Caebar in Dâr Tabib","'Our return to the city... was not uneventful. My sister... will speak of it to you.'","Talk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib","Retrieve Corudan's notes about the Fearwater from the satchel at the foot of his bed","Caebar thinks for a moment about what you have shown him.","Caebar is in Dâr Tabib.","'${PLAYER}, my friend... my wound is well on its way to healing... but to see you return with victory... eases the pain. I understand Umbar has been saved from... Nakási and Balakhâd? Has Gondor too... escaped from their wrath?'\
\
You tell Corudan that King Elessar and his soldiers fought bravely against the Song, and Gondor survived. He smiles weakly.\
\
'Then the last of Sauron's schemes... has been frustrated, ${PLAYER}. I am glad for my part in it...'\
\
You insist that Corudan rest, and you will speak with him when he is more fully healed.","Caebar flushes.\
\
'Oh! I am sorry to interrupt, ${PLAYER}! I did not know you had returned! I have visited our friends every day while Corudan recovers, and they have spoken to me of your adventure in the Fearwater.\
\
'Please, finish your visit! I will speak with you afterward.'","Talk to Corudan in Dâr Tabib","Corudan lies in one of the beds of Dâr Tabib.","The Apothecary of Dâr Tabib is located in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.","Wait for Caebar to speak again","'You should visit them at Dâr Tabib, in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl. I know Corudan and Sigileth will be pleased to see you!'","'I understand Nakási is slain and the Song of Waves and Wind defeated, ${PLAYER}. May there now be peace for a time!\
\
'I heard tell that five ships of the Song survived the passage to Gondor, and waged war upon the Harlond? More might have joined them, had the rapids of the Ikorbân not proved too perilous; we saw the ruin of many smaller ships dashed upon the rocks as we travelled this way from Sûg Nidar. The builders of the fleet likely intended that to be a one-way voyage, but they had not counted upon Cúridwan's damaging solution, or your great haste in opposing those who escaped it.\
\
'The raft-bridge of the Wrackwade did not last long against the Narghâk cannons. When we rejoined Rahâzi at Iridír she said her mother intended to see it rebuilt. It would not surprise me to learn she has already done so! But I have gotten ahead of myself. There is more to tell.\
\
'While you pursued the Song toward Umbar, my brother and I and Cúridwan made our own way westward. Our return journey... was not uneventful.'","Epilogue: A Mending","Sigileth watches over her brother in Dâr Tabib.","Talk to Caebar in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib","Talk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib and hear her account of their return to the city","'I cannot say with certainty that the spirit was Silirtas, or that she heard my words. But I believe it was, and she did. I will not hurry to join her, but when at last I come to that place, I hope she and I will reside in comfort and in peace, beyond the loneliness and fear that so troubled Silirtas when she contemplated the unknown days ahead.\
\
'That is my desire, ${PLAYER}. I cannot know if it will come to pass, but if hope leads us ever onward, the pleasant dream of it will live in my heart until the last of my days arrives.'","Many of the beds of Dâr Tabib are occupied by the wounded","You retrieve a sheaf of Corudan's notes from the satchel","'Look for these papers among Corudan's belongings, and give them to Caebar.'","The recent upheavals scarred the city, but now it begins to heal, as do some of the companions who fought by your side.","Someone new has come to Dâr Tabib","Enter the Apothecary of Dâr Tabib in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl","Sigileth is in Dâr Tabib.","Bring Corudan's notes to Caebar in Dâr Tabib","'Yes, I will tell you what transpired after you left us.'","'The Kindred of the Coins was neither entirely evil nor entirely good, ${PLAYER}. Like Hyarmendacil II, they achieved both lasting good and enduring harm. Does one erase the other? Wiser scholars than I may be able to weigh the value of each... but I cannot. Must we forget the instrumental roles played by Azagath and Nakási in the freeing of Umbar from the Heirs of Castamir and the cultists of Sauron? Must we forget Khôltekh's deeds during the Dagor Carlanthir, or Hármelak's advice that Dâr Laja be opened to the needs of her people? Must their later crimes strike from the record their earlier heroics and wise governance?'\
\
Caebar studies the ground intently.\
\
'Must my mother's refusal to see me erase the happy years I spent as a child in Ethring, ${PLAYER}? I think it cannot. So we celebrate the good and we work to remedy the bad, and by so doing we mend what wounds we can, and seek to avoid inflicting further harm. That is healing, of a kind, is it not?'\
\
The Gondorian scribe heaves a sigh and looks up at you again, forcing a smile.\
\
'From conversation with the Umbari I have sketched the members of the original Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}. Umbar will remember both their fine qualities and their faults, neither excusing the other, and with these drawings I hoped to capture that balance. Choose one of your liking and it is yours; the others I will give to the city of Umbar Baharbêl, that it may remember its history and not forget it.'","Caebar bids farewell to Corudan and Sigileth and departs Dâr Tabib","Caebar stands in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.","'Caebar has visited every day, and kept us informed of events in the city.'","Caebar emerges from his musings with a nod","Caebar accepts the papers and briefly studies them.\
\
'Wait... you say that Corudan found these in an Ordâkh encampment in the Fearwater? I do not want to pester him with questions, ${PLAYER}, so let us speak of this outside.'","You find Caebar excitedly studying the papers Corudan retrieved from the Ordâkhai of Sûg Nidar.\
\
'The soldiers would not have understood the meaning of this parchment, ${PLAYER}, but I do. They must have found it among the ruins of Kasukhín while searching for treasure; thinking it unimportant, they kept it unguarded among their belongings, where it went overlooked until it was picked up by Corudan.\
\
'These are the words of Vinyarion, twenty-fourth King of Gondor, who bore the title of Hyarmendacil II: \\qthe South-victor.\\q Set down by a trusted retainer in his old age, only days before his death, these words claim that he repented of his long campaign in Harad, and wept at the bones of Shâraban, a city he destroyed in the days of his youth. On the return journey of his tenth pilgrimage to the lands he once conquered, he rested at the hilltop fort of Kasukhín and died there, peacefully, in his sleep. Sigileth tells me the land around that fort is now changed, and what was once a hill is now an island; might Vinyarion's bones lie there to this day, kept isolated from discovery by the creation of the Fearwater?\
\
'His story raises complicated emotions in my heart, ${PLAYER}; he is considered very differently in Shagâna than he is in Gondor, and it is difficult to reconcile those two perspectives. I am put in mind of the relationship the Umbari must now have with the Kindred of the Coins that preceded the Ghad Imghêda, the Kindred Redeemed.'","Corudan's possessions can be found in the satchel at the foot of his bed.","'They returned to the city a few days ago and now recover in Dâr Tabib. You can find this apothecary in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.'","'That reminds me. My brother collected some papers from the Ordâkhai while we adventured in the Fearwater. He intended to give them to Caebar, but the matter has slipped our minds until now. Look for them among Corudan's belongings, and give them to Caebar.'","And as a light breeze passes over the sea, thus ends 'The Song of Waves and Wind'"},
[4806]={"Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","'Ah, what is this?!'\
\
Cánnakh points at one of his parchments.\
\
'This old story tells a tale of a strange beast called Amardam, who became lost in the Duvuinen Swamp. It was difficult to translate this old parchment but from the description, it sounds like a Caerog! If this old tale holds true, awaking an ancient Caerog would indeed be a great power. In the wrong hands, an ancient Caerog would bring absolute destruction to these lands.\
\
'Quickly, head to the Duvuinen Swamp and search there for anything strange. We must defeat this Caerog before it is too late!'","Cánnakh has located the lost power, a Caerog buried in the Duvuinen Swamp. He asks for you to wake and defeat the slumbering evil before someone else finds it and Amardam regains its full strength.","Habla con Cánnakh","Defeat Amardam","Epilogue: Amardam, the Ancient Evil","Defeated Amardam","The rocks begin to move as the Caerog springs to life","'Ah, I was right! The story had some truth in it!\
\
'It seems that in ancient times, this Caerog sank into the swamp, awaiting to be awakened. I wonder if it was defeated by some ancient hero? Alas, some stories will remain hidden.\
\
'You have done a great service to the people of Aughaire and give hope to the rest of the Free People in Angmar.'","Amardam can be found somewhere in the Duvuinen Swamp.\
\
You should awake and defeat Amardam."},
[4807]={"'I think I have seen this shape before. I cannot be certain, but... yes, it is worth a try! It will take me some time to dig it out again, but if you go to one of the metalworkers of Járnfast, I will meet you once I find it. Wait for me by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast. There you will find the best, and the fastest, of Járnfast's metalworkers.'","Wait for the metalworker to forge a key using the mould","'I see the matter of the broken key has captured your interest, as it has mine. I have studied it closely, but that examination revealed no distinguishing marks upon its surface, and no clue to its origin. The top of the key appears to have been broken off, but several teeth remain. Not enough to match the key with a particular lock, however, and unlikely to open it should we chance upon the correct one. Pity.\
\
'I will give it back to you, with the hope that you may find someone who knows about this key, or others like it.'\
\
Gandalf leans on his staff and looks away over the encampment.\
\
'I have been thinking about Gothmog's words. He said he was given this key by a Morgul-slave, and it would unlock a weapon that could not be overcome? I cannot imagine what this weapon might be, but we must not let it fall into the hands of evil. And there is another thing, ${PLAYER}. I get the sense that Gothmog himself did not know what this key might unlock. If he knew the location of such a weapon, would he not claim it at once? But he told you he searched in vain.\
\
'There is something peculiar about all this. Good luck, friend.'","'My work is finished. I suppose you should bring the newly-forged key to Khîl Tale-spinner.'","'I found it, ${PLAYER}! When I was cleaning out my father's home, I chanced upon this mould and a small locked box. I thought little of these artifacts, and put them away with the rest of the odds and ends. But look at this!'\
\
Khîl holds out a small casting mould with a hollow in the shape of a key. The broken key given to you by Gothmog rests comfortably within the indentation.\
\
'Using this mould, the metalworkers here could fashion a duplicate of this key, and I warrant it will unlock the box I found, or I am no Zhélruka! Give the mould and these instructions to this fine dwarf, and once the key is forged I will meet you back in the hidden chamber!'","The metalworker hands you the newly-forged key","Khîl Tale-spinner hurries toward you, and the metalworker falls silent","Metalworkers can be found on the lower level of Járnfast.","'Gothmog said he was given this key by a Morgul-slave, and it would unlock a weapon that could not be overcome? I cannot imagine what this weapon might be, but we must not let it fall into the hands of evil. And there is another thing, ${PLAYER}. I get the sense that Gothmog himself did not know what this key might unlock. If he knew the location of such a weapon, would he not claim it at once? But he told you he searched in vain.\
\
'There is something peculiar about all this. Good luck, friend.'","Khîl Tale-spinner has returned to the hidden chamber built by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin.","The newly-forged key should now be ready","The key clicks in the lock. Inside the box you find a small shard of glass, and nothing else","Is it possible that Khîl Tale-spinner might know something about the broken key given to you by Gothmog?","'This should not take long. I will have a new key forged for you in just a short while.'","'The bones of Isildur have come part of the way, but I travelled ahead of the waggon to once again test Grimbeorn's hospitality. He is prone to grumbling, but the meals he serves are without compare on this side of the Misty Mountains. Did you learn anything about the broken key given to you by Gothmog?'\
\
You tell Gandalf what transpired in Járnfast and show him the glass shard you obtained from the locked box in Khîl's home. He studies it closely.\
\
'Hmm... a broken piece of glass? This does not appear to be a weapon of any kind. Is it possible Gothmog's key might have unlocked more than one container? Unless...'\
\
Gandalf holds the shard up to his eye and squints through it.\
\
'The glass is cloudy, as if it contains something which obscures my vision. It moves from side to side as I stare at it, almost like...'\
\
Gandalf looks up suddenly, and clutches at the Black Book hanging from his belt. He flips it open and peers through the shard of glass at one weathered page.\
\
'There is hidden writing here, ${PLAYER}! It is as I suspected from the very outset! I did not think we could find the means to reveal it, but you have done so!'","The metalworkers are by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast.","Khîl gives you the mould that matches the broken key","'A shard of glass, no more than a hand's breadth in size? This is the treasure? I do not know what I expected, ${PLAYER}, but I expected more than this! It seems quite ordinary. Why would anyone lock this away, and then break the key?\
\
'You told me you were acquainted with Gandalf the Wizard. Perhaps he will know what to make of this broken glass, if there is anything to make of it. I fear you will be wasting his time, but if you think he will not mind it you should ask him anyway. Where has he gone?'\
\
You tell Khîl that Gandalf recently spent some time in the lands far to the south, but the Wizard intended to journey north once again alongside a waggon. He is likely to be at the Beorninghús by now.","Unlock the tiny locked box in the hidden chamber","Khîl Tale-spinner is in the hidden chamber built by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin.","'Well? Does the key fit in the lock or not?'","Talk to a metalworker by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast","'Have you learned anything about the broken key?'","'Yes, what can I do for you?'\
\
The metalworker looks at you with surprise.\
\
'You mean you don't know? Oh, you're waiting for someone. Khîl Tale-spinner? This suddenly makes a great deal of sense. That Zhélruka...'","Talk to Khîl Tale-spinner by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast","Gandalf may know what to make of the strange glass shard. Look for him at the Beorninghús","Bring the glass shard to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Gandalf intended to travel north with the casket containing the bones of Isildur, and should have arrived at the Beorninghús by now. You should bring him the glass shard you found within the tiny locked box from Khîl's home.","Find someone who knows about the broken key","Give the broken key to Khîl Tale-spinner in the hidden chamber","'Disturb me not while I work! This may look easy, but I assure you it is not!'","'What a surprise, my friend! I did not expect to see you again, and because we are so close I will forgive your unheralded intrusion into my home! Ah, just a jest, a jest! You are welcome here at any time. How goes the examination of the Black Book written by my thrice-great grandfather Vóin? Do not forget that it belongs to me, and if it proves valuable I would welcome payment equivalent to its value.'\
\
Khîl gestures at the runes on the walls.\
\
'When we first discovered this place it frightened me, but I have found myself coming in here more and more often. I find that the aura here calms and relaxes me. It is not so for Lord Náin! He is still not happy about this chamber, but it is so old and my claim to this home of my forebears is so clear that he dares not do anything about it. For that the Lord of the Iron Hills has my respect, and the stillness of my tongue. Many are the stories I might tell of him were it otherwise, true tales all, though he might not agree. So everyone is happy!\
\
'But what brings you here, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You show Khîl the broken key, and he studies it carefully.\
\
'Do you know something? I think I have seen this shape before. I cannot be certain, but... yes, it is worth a try! It will take me some time to dig it out again, but if you go to one of the metalworkers of Járnfast, I will meet you once I find it. Wait for me by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast, ${PLAYER}. There you will find the best, and the fastest, of Járnfast's metalworkers.'","The metalworker is by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast. He should have finished forging the key by now.","'Here you go. May this key unlock whatever it is you seek to unlock.\
\
'If the container be of Zhélruka make, perhaps it is better for me to hope that this key will properly lock it away, and rid us of whatever madness Khîl Tale-spinner weaves now!'","You must find someone who knows what the broken key might once have unlocked. But who could hold that secret?","'I think you will be wasting the Wizard's time with this. It is just a piece of broken glass. How disappointing!'","'I will meet you back at the hidden chamber when the key is forged!'","Epilogue: An Incomplete Key","Gothmog gave you a broken key as he died, but you do not know what it might have unlocked when whole. Unless your guess is wrong, it seems as if Gothmog himself did not know.","Khîl Tale-spinner is by the forges in Járnfast.","Talk to the metalworker by the forges in Járnfast","Talk to Khîl in the hidden chamber in his home","The metalworker needs some time to fashion a new key using the mould provided by Khîl Tale-spinner.","Give the mould to the metalworker by the forges in Járnfast","Khîl told you about a tiny locked box that he thought his mother used to store jewels, but perhaps it is far older than that...\
\
He has placed it on the table in the hidden chamber, and waits for you to try the newly-forged key in its lock.","Khîl Tale-spinner smiles a greeting at you as you approach","'The key is forged? Then let us see if it opens the box I found in the same place as the mould. I assumed the box belonged to my mother and contained her decorative jewels, but perhaps it is not so.\
\
'I have set it on the table there.'"},
[4808]={"Epilogue: Closing the Book","Together, you and Gandalf have managed to reveal the last of the secrets hidden within the Black Book of Mordor, and the only remaining question concerns the matter of its final disposition.","'Hello again, my friend! Did the kingsfoil I give to you cure your headaches? I have some more here if you... oh, you are not here for kingsfoil? What brings you then to the Houses of Lore?'\
\
You explain to Covadil that you have come into possession of a book that has much to say concerning the history of Gondor and you would like it to find a place on the shelves among other such tomes. You hand her the glass shard and begin to describe the account contained within the pages of the Black Book, but before you have gone very far Covadil interrupts with an apologetic smile.\
\
'It isn't really up to me, but I can give the book to the masters, and they will study it for acceptability. If they deem it merits inclusion, and truly does contain knowledge of use to Gondor, they will add it to the collection.'\
\
You wonder aloud whether any of the scholars in the Houses of Lore can read ancient Zhélruka runes.\
\
'Oh, I doubt it,' she responds. 'I think I will just add it to the shelves myself. If you say this contains important historical knowledge, I believe you! None today can say what might be important to know for tomorrow! I say we preserve this tome for future scholars to mull over!'\
\
Covadil takes the Black Book from you and carefully tucks the glass shard inside the cover.\
\
'I look forward to reading it, ${PLAYER}! I have been trying to decide which language I should next set my sights upon, and it seems I have received my course: the runes of the ancient Zhélruka! Thank you once again, my friend! The Black Book will remain here in the Houses of Lore, waiting to enrich the knowledge of future interested scholars, and I am glad to have played a part in it!'","Deliver the Black Book to Covadil in the Houses of Lore","Deliver the Black Book to Karazgar by the flat stone at the Old Ford","'And so ends the Black Book of Mordor,' Gandalf murmurs with satisfaction","'Yes, ${PLAYER}, I have been expecting you. Together we have unearthed every secret hidden within the Black Book of Mordor by Vóin and Bozhéna, the long-distant dwarves who authored it. Only one question remains: what is to be done with the book now?\
\
'I see a number of possibilities, my friend. It was Khîl Tale-spinner who gave the book into our keeping, and his claim is perhaps the strongest. Vóin and Bozhéna were his thrice-great grandparents, and if the book is to be kept by anyone still living today in Middle-earth, we might do worse than a Zhélruka relative of its authors.\
\
'But there is another interest to be considered. The Black Book of Mordor contains a great deal of information that would be prized by scholars concerning the history of Gondor and the fate of King Eärnur. The book is truly deserving of a place of honour in the Houses of Lore in Minas Tirith. The scholar Covadil would gratefully accept the donation of it, and in that way Vóin's wish for Eärnur's struggle to be remembered in the future will truly be fulfilled.\
\
'There is one other claim to the Black Book, ${PLAYER}. Indeed, the nobility of this claim might be doubted, but I believe it is still worth considering. I speak of the claim of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, who asked that you steal the book and deliver it to him. Yes, I knew of your encounter with him at the Old Ford. I chose not to say anything, but I am pleased my trust in you was not misplaced, and we were able to decipher the last of the book's mysteries.\
\
'Why then might we entertain Karazgar's request, ${PLAYER}? Why, it is for that very reason: we know what the book says, and he does not. He believes it contains the secret to preventing his decline, or securing his power... but it does not. It does contain a great deal of confusion and mystery for one who does not know how to read it, and that is to say nothing of the trick with the shard of beacon-glass. What might he give up in exchange for a book he thinks will be of use to him, but is not, and cannot be? It may be an academic question, but those are always of great interest to me.\
\
'So I leave the disposition of the Black Book of Mordor to you, my friend. Choose who should have it, and deliver it either to Khîl Tale-spinner in Járnfast, Covadil in the Houses of Lore in Minas Tirith, or Karazgar at the Old Ford. I leave the decision up to you, and with this choice we will close the Black Book of Mordor for good. I thank you again, ${PLAYER}.'","'Welcome back, my friend! Were you able to solve the mystery of the glass-shard and Vóin's book? Did Gandalf have any ideas?'\
\
For a number of hours you describe what you learned from the secret writing in the Black Book, and conclude at last that your need for the tome has ended.\
\
'You are giving it back to me? Well, I thank you for this! It seems that it properly belongs here in the chamber Vóin built, and with your assurance that it is not truly a tome of evil, I should think it will be quite safe to keep it here!\
\
'Like my thrice-great grandmother Bozhéna, I too have found the aura of this hidden chamber to be one of peace and comfort. I am quite pleased to know more of these relatives of mine, who once were mere names, but now are much more than that! And to think my thrice-great grandfather Vóin defied the Witch-king himself, and not only that, but he may have at last ended his days in the halls of Thafar-gathol itself!\
\
'Now that is a tale, ${PLAYER}. That is a tale indeed! Thank you for upholding your end of the bargain and delivering the Black Book back into my keeping, where it belongs. You will be my friend for always, good ${RACE}.'","'I leave the disposition of the Black Book of Mordor to you, my friend. Choose who should have it, and deliver it either to Khîl Tale-spinner in Járnfast, Covadil in the Houses of Lore in Minas Tirith, or Karazgar at the Old Ford. I leave the decision up to you, and with this choice we will close the Black Book of Mordor for good. I thank you again, ${PLAYER}.'","Gandalf gave you the choice of where to bring the Black Book and you have now performed that duty.","Deliver the Black Book to Khîl Tale-spinner in his home","Gandalf has presented you with a choice concerning the ultimate disposition of the Black Book of Mordor.","You stand at the Old Ford and resolve to wait for Karazgar to appear.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>"},
[4809]={"Durin has come to Mótsog's Tomb to speak with the last of the Greymauls before the day is ended.","Durin is in Mótsog's Tomb, thinking about the words of the last Greymaul.","Durin's face is burdened with expectation as he waits for Mótsog's response","'Where has Mótsog gone? I wished to speak with him before the day was ended.\
\
'It is not too late, is it? Will you come with me, ${PLAYER}? Let us find him in the chamber beneath Gundabad, if it is not already too late. There is something I wished to ask him, and I will regret it if I do not!'","Durin is in Mótsog's Tomb, thinking about the road that brought him here... and the road that still lies ahead.","Talk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb","Wait for Durin to arrive","And so concludes 'The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves'","Durin awaits Mótsog's reply, and does not speak.","The last of the Greymauls has left the world. Only his statue remains","Talk to Mótsog and hear his response","'My dream is ending, Durin. I will watch no more.\
\
'Your fate is your own, and will be the result of the choices you make. Whether those may lead to good ends or ill will be up to you, and to those who stand with you.\
\
'But I have seen our kind face innumerable trials during the long years of my vigil. It is the belief of this dwarf that you will have success, in this age or the next, though it seem far away and nearly impossible to achieve.\
\
'Farewell, Durin, both my oldest friend and my newest. Farewell.'","'We are not too late, ${PLAYER}, but I deem his time is short.'\
\
Durin addresses the silent figure.\
\
'Mótsog, I cannot forgive you for the treachery in your past, but I acknowledge the aid you provided to the Gabil'akkâ in the reclamation of Gundabad. For that you have not only my gratitude but that of every dwarf whose heart longed for the Mountain-home to be restored. So too do you have the thanks of dwarves not yet born, who will now know a world where Gundabad will never again be held by the Orcs.'\
\
Durin nods, that business accomplished. When next he speaks his voice is tinged with curiosity and worry.\
\
'This question is for me, Mótsog, not as a prince or a king to be, but as a dwarf only. Did you see in your dream whether I would one day have victory in Khazad-dûm? I would have us reclaim it, as we have with Gundabad... but I cannot tell if only failure awaits us as it did the Iron Garrison, and Balin before.'","Durin wants to speak with Mótsog before the day is ended.","The entrance to the secret stair that leads to Mótsog's Tomb, deep below Gundabad, is in Zul-mazal.","Epilogue: Endings and Beginnings","Mótsog is gone, and only a statue remains.","Examine the statue of Mótsog","Return to Mótsog's Tomb at the bottom of the secret stair beneath Zul-mazal","Durin studies the statue where Mótsog once stood.","Durin hurries to Mótsog's Tomb to speak with the last of the Greymauls before the day comes to an end.","'Good-bye, Mótsog. Once I called you friend, and once enemy. Let us part now as friends, for there will be no chance more to make it otherwise.\
\
'Take your rest, last of the Greymauls, and know that on this, your last day, you were a son of Gundabad, and a proud dwarf.'","'He is gone.'\
\
Durin sighs deeply and peers around the now-empty chamber.\
\
'Whatever distant sight was given to Mótsog by the First Crafter is gone with him, ${PLAYER}. I thought he might have advised me one way or the other, and so help me make this choice: should Khazad-dûm stay lost to us, or is it to be my task to reclaim it? But he guided me not.\
\
'And yet, I still feel comforted by his words. Why should that be so? Perhaps it is because it is as he said: those who stand with me will lend me their courage. One day, perhaps, it will fall to me to lead another union of dwarves to the Doors of Durin, and on that day Khazad-dûm will belong to dwarves forevermore.\
\
'In this age or the next, did he say? Let us work together, then, and see that the age that comes will be one of peace and prosperity for all the good folk of this Middle-earth!'\
\
Durin takes one more look around the chamber and hefts the Red Axe in his hand.\
\
'And in the end, perhaps the lesson of Mótsog will be this: not all stories end when they seem to, but rather they continue, and you cannot fully judge one's part in it during the telling! Both good acts and evil shape the world, in Gundabad no more nor less than anywhere else, and it is the duty of good-hearted folk to care for those who dwell in it. Will you take up this duty with me, my friend, and make that the legacy we leave behind?'\
\
You assure Durin that he can rely on you.\
\
'Very good, ${PLAYER}. We will begin in Gundabad, and who knows where else the adventure will take us? But we will meet it gladly, with courage in our hearts and our eyes on the horizon.'"},
[4811]={"The shade of Isildur fades from view","'Hearing the tale of Tárandil in its fullness fills me with both satisfaction and regret, ${PLAYER}. The first for the responses in it to questions long unanswered, but the second for my own part in the tale. The evil deeds he performed cannot be excused, but if I had known the full extent of the shade's story I might have stayed my hand. Farewell to Tárandil, and to Bravantel and Héol, whatever their fates.\
\
'Our journey must continue, ${PLAYER}. One oath may yet be fulfilled. We must continue on to Rivendell.'","His vow fulfilled, the shade of Isildur at last knows peace","Talk to the shade of Isildur at the entrance to Rivendell","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad","Talk to Gandalf by the entrance to Rivendell and complete 'Instance: Freed of the Burden'","The shade of Tárandil fades from view","'I do not forgive you, Tárandil, my son not of blood but of choice. But I think there was a time when these sorrows might have been avoided, had you spoken freely to me in life.\
\
'I set aside my vengeance. There is no suffering I could impose that you have not inflicted upon yourself. Go then, and endure the punishment you earned, the punishment you created. Begone.'","The shade of Tárandil has made his decision: he will seek out Bravantel and Héol, no matter the torment it will cause him.","'At last.'","Talk to the shade of Isildur by the waggon in Laerlad","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward, in Laerlad.","'Hemos llegado.'","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon near the entrance to Rivendell","The waggon bearing the bones of Isildur has come a long way from Gondor, and so have you","The shade of Isildur is by the waggon bearing his bones northward, in Laerlad.","'After the passage of so many years I have come at last to Rivendell, ${PLAYER}, as was my vow. I can now know rest, these long centuries later. Never did I think this day would come!'\
\
The shade of Isildur wavers before you, shimmering in and out of view. With a great effort, he remains to give you his final words.\
\
'The tale of Tárandil has stirred something in me, and I can dismiss it no longer. I know the struggle he faced, the conflict that caused him such distress, and I find I can understand. I do not forgive him! But I understand what caused him to fall. He was my son, not of blood, but a son all the same. Some measure of his wickedness must be traced to me, for was I not the man he would strive to be?'\
\
The shade of Isildur wavers again, his attachment to Middle-earth made tenuous by fulfilment of his ancient vow.\
\
'My thoughts turn to Eärnur, ${PLAYER}. Tárandil fell to darkness through the arts of the Blade of Lebennin, one of the Nazgûl, and not the greatest nor the most evil. But Eärnur fell to the Lord of the Nazgûl himself. Eärnur spoke of the torments he endured in that dark place, and I dismissed them! The blood of my brother Anárion ran through his veins, and I chastened him for not resisting! I cursed him for failure... I, who might have ended the reign of Sauron forever, and could not!\
\
'I regret my words. Eärnur should not be left to rot within Minas Morgul, ${PLAYER}. Did I say he died as Gothmog? Nay. He died as Eärnur, descended through many generations from my brother Anárion, who perished on the fields before Barad-dûr. It is my hope that the body of Eärnur will be recovered, and given a king's rest. This is my final request, ${PLAYER}. Farewell.'","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones to Rivendell, by the entrance to that secret valley.","The shade of Isildur has at last finished the journey he swore in life to undertake more than three thousand years ago.","The shade of Tárandil bows his head and fades from view","Epilogue: Freed of the Burden","'Both Isildur and the Ring came to Rivendell, long years after he so vowed, and now both are gone from the world. It has been an eventful journey. But there is one more thing I must say to you, my friend.'\
\
Gandalf's eye twinkles merrily, and he lifts the Black Book of Mordor from its leather strap.\
\
'I spent the latter half of the ride to Rivendell considering what I might have missed within the Black Book, ${PLAYER}. The glass shard from the beacon of Barad Cúron revealed no further secrets to me, but I felt certain there was more to learn. Had I overlooked some trick? At last I have determined my error, and while I am ashamed to admit it, even the very wise will sometimes make mistakes of this fashion. I was so focused upon the writing of Vóin that all else was obscured, as if I were blindfolded. That is how I missed it!\
\
'Vóin's hand-writing is very distinctive, and as I scoured it for any further clue, I quite ignored the drawings which decorate the margins of several pages near the end of the tome. I saw no meaning in these pictures, for I thought them mere embellishment. And yet... hidden among these illustrations I finally recognized further dwarf-runes! I did not see them during my previous studies because they were not written in Vóin's hand. Someone else wrote these runes, hiding them in plain sight!\
\
'I have now translated them, ${PLAYER}, and can properly tell you the ending to Vóin's tale. Are you ready to finish our study of the Black Book of Mordor, and close it for good?'","Through the telling of his tale, the shade of Tárandil has achieved the clarity he had lost. It is time for another of the shades that has remained overlong in Middle-earth to find his own respite.","'Our journey must continue to Rivendell, ${PLAYER}. One oath may yet be fulfilled.'","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones to Rivendell, by the entrance to that secret valley. He has finished reading the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor, and wishes to tell you the end of that tale.","'That is all Bozhéna has to say to us, ${PLAYER}. I am pleased to know the end of the tale. Now with the departure of Isildur our business in Rivendell is concluded; Aragorn will have need of us in Gondor, for evil still lurks within Minas Morgul.'\
\
Reminded of Isildur's last request, you tell Gandalf that the son of Elendil repented of his words concerning Eärnur, and hoped his body might be recovered from Barad Cúron. Gandalf mirthfully raises an eyebrow.\
\
'It has already been done, ${PLAYER}. Aragorn, that is to say King Elessar, commanded that Eärnur's body be recovered from Minas Morgul before I began the northward journey to Rivendell.'\
\
You ask Gandalf the reason behind Elessar's command.\
\
'Actually, it was quite simple. \\qEärnur was a king of Gondor,\\q he said to me. \\qHe should return to the land he loved, and that loved him.\\q\
\
'I saw the wisdom in it, and did not gainsay his words. Within the hour, guards of the Citadel were dispatched to Barad Cúron to carry out the king's command. They found the watching-stones outside the tower abandoned, and passed within without objection. Eärnur's body was borne from the city and returned to Minas Tirith. He was laid to rest in the tomb of his fathers on the Silent Street, and at last he knew freedom from the shadows of Mordor and the long reach of Angmar.'\
\
Gandalf nods thoughtfully, and raps his staff upon the ground.\
\
'Well! I think that is story enough for one journey! I thank you once again for your company on this long road, my friend, and I shall seek for you when next I have cause. Until then, farewell! Should you have need of me before then, look for me at the lodge of our good friend Grimbeorn, whose hospitality cannot be measured!'","'I desired to confess my treachery, and I have done so. There remains but one thing for me.\
\
'I will seek for my wife and child, for Bravantel and Héol, no matter where they may be. I would suffer any hurt to see them again, and to know their fate, whether it be doom undeterred or rest finally achieved. Do they linger still in this world? I have to know. If I must consign myself to mindless oblivion in the effort, so be it. I face it without fear.'\
\
Tárandil's form wavers uncertainly, and he addresses Isildur for the last time.\
\
'Father, I do not seek your pardon. I know it could never be granted, and I would not ask it. But I wanted you to know how sorry I am. I have forgotten so much over the centuries, but that I never lost. That sorrow was always with me, even when all else was emptiness.'","After a brief rest, the waggon will return to Gondor","'The runes hidden within the embellishments on some of these pages are written in the Zhélruka mode, but not in Vóin's distinctive hand.\
\
'No, these letters were made by another: Vóin's wife Bozhéna. It was she who finished the Black Book of Mordor. Hear now her words, and you will know the end of the tale herein contained.'","Meet up with Gandalf and the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur at the entrance to the valley of Rivendell","Gandalf suggested you catch up with the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur when it arrives at the entrance to the valley of Rivendell."},
[4812]={"Epilogue: His Father's Son","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Tárandil, and says nothing.","The shade of Tárandil is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","'Much has been made clear to me by Tárandil's confession.'\
\
Gandalf leans wearily on his staff.\
\
'The shade of Isildur spoke true. The Disaster of the Gladden Fields was no accident.'","'Tárandil's confession has not yet ended. If he will say more, we must listen.'","Talk to the shade of Tárandil and complete 'Instance: His Father's Son'","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","The shade of Tárandil has manifested for a single purpose: he wishes to make his confession.","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad","'What says Tárandil now? His confession is not complete.'","'I have more to tell, though it cause me pain. I heed it not, for the wounds run deep; there is no part of me that feels them not.'"},
[4813]={"Talk to the shade of Isildur beside the waggon in Laerlad","'Have you forgotten why I came this way, ${PLAYER}? I am here in the Vales of Anduin as escort for the waggon bearing Isildur's bones northward! Yes, the son of Elendil will at last complete the journey he began at the start of the Age, and by so doing see the fulfilment of his oath! I left the waggon to partake of Grimbeorn's hospitality, for his dogs serve a merry feast, but it is past time for this Wizard to return to service. And you should come with me! Are you not tied up in this business as well?\
\
'Do not give me that look. I had very little to do with your getting involved, if you remember. I daresay I could not have stopped you, had I the mind to try. I will see you alongside the waggon. The driver should have reached Laerlad by now. Look for him along the road beside the Gladden Fields.'","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad","Talk to Vágari the Wanderer","Vágari the Wanderer has come to this place, enveloped by a feeling of dread","Epilogue: Isildur's Last Journey","'Stand by the waggon and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for the source of this dread. It may be nothing, but it also may not.'","'Something is not right. Something here is amiss.'","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones through Laerlad.","The shade of Isildur feels the presence of his bones, and follows with interest their northward course along the river.","The waggon bearing Isildur's bones is in Laerlad, on the road beside the Gladden Fields.","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones, near to the Gladden Fields.","'The source of the dread has become visible to us. How curious.'","Gandalf journeyed north ahead of the waggon bearing Isildur's bones, and he thinks it is time to check on its progress.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for the source of the dread by the waggon","Find the waggon carrying Isildur's bones on the road through Laerlad, beside the Gladden Fields","A sensation of dread surrounds the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur","Gandalf has directed you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for the source of the dread near the waggon bearing Isildur's bones.","'I know. I know. I know. Son-of-no-blood, son-of-no-blood!'\
\
The shade stares past you, glaring at the waggon, and the dread sensation intensifies. Then it abates, with only emptiness left in its wake.\
\
'I remember now,' the shade murmurs. 'It was lost to me, but now it has returned. I know what I saw. I know what I did.'\
\
The shade grows indistinct, wavering in your vision, and then reforms again. It seems to take a great deal of effort, and leaves Vágari weary.\
\
'I want to confess to you what I saw, and what I did. I want one among the living to know of my misdeeds. And then there is something I must do. Will you heed me?'","'Something is not right. Something is amiss.\
\
'I sense the presence of evil. I am beyond harm... have I not suffered harm enough in these lands? But I would have no further injury come to my remains! Whatever evil comes here, begone! Take thee from these lands, and leave us be!'","'The source of the dread has become visible to us, and wishes to confess its crimes? I find this most peculiar, ${PLAYER}, and I urge you to remain on guard. We must not forget this is a creature of evil.\
\
'But I think we should hear what it has to say.'","Talk to Gandalf beside the waggon in Laerlad","Vágari the Wanderer has appeared by the waggon. But why has he chosen to appear now?","'I will see you alongside the waggon. The driver should have reached the road through Laerlad by now, beside the Gladden Fields.'","'There is a dreadful presence here, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot see the source of it. I advise you to stand by the waggon and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for the source of this dread. It may be nothing, but it also may not.'"},
[4814]={"Treasures of the Second Age can be found in Western Gondor and the Paths of the Dead.\
\
You should seek out the five treasures of the Second Age.","The trinket was once a necklace of the king of the mountain","The amethyst represented the honour of Dunharrow","Drugât leaves you in hopes of one day to finally be at rest","Speak with Drugât","Find the Second Age Crown","The crown symbolized the oath we took for Isildur","Drugât is located in the caverns of Nimrond.\
\
You should return the Second Age treasures to Drugât.","Drugât wishes to reclaim that which should have been rightfully returned to him by Isildur.","Find the Second Age Amethyst","Epilogue: Restless Souls","'Ah, these objects hold much history to the men of Dunharrow. It has been such a long time. You have held your word and for once, I will uphold mine. I leave you now and hope to never see you or any living creature, again.'","Drugât wished to speak with you instead of fighting","Drugât has returned to the Vale and must be banished once and for all.","'Drugât has returned to the Vale! It is true, I have seen him with my own eyes near Dâr Matum. I did not think he would try anything more after we defeated him in Nimrond. This explains the recent movement of dead and Orcs. He must be secretly planning something in the dark recesses of Nimrond.\
\
'Will you venture to Nimrond and vanquish Drugât once and for all?'","Drugât is located somewhere in the caverns of Nimrond.\
\
You should speak with Drugât.","Find the Second Age Ingot","Find and confront Drugât","Find the Second Age Rune","Find the Second Age Trinket","The rune told the history of Dunharrow","Drugât is located somewhere in the caverns of Nimrond.\
\
You should find and confront Drugât.","The ingot represented the strength of the Men of the Mountain","Return the Second Age treasures to Drugât","'Listen to me, ${RACE}, and hear my story. I no longer wish to be a part of this conflict. My scouts from the east have learned of Nerzus' demise. That same fate besieges me if I am to travel further into the coming storm. I followed the Dark Lord so long ago, I am not sure why I chose to follow him again. No good came from it, only death and restlessness for all time. If he had true power over his subjects, he would have freed us from this curse ages ago.\
\
'I will leave this Vale and return to the mountains. First though, I ask a favour of you. When Isildur met with us, I gave him a gift as collateral for our oath of allegiance. Since the oath had been broken, the treasures were never returned. If you find these ancient treasures and return them to me, I shall leave Gondor in peace and command these restless men of Dunharrow to do the same.'"},
[4815]={"DNT -- will not be seen","Search near Hata Kebir for Jajax and Daxamat","Jajax can be found along the coastline to the south of Aerthir.\
\
You have discovered Jajax and Daxamat resting from readying their ship, and should speak to them.","Search the shores of the Anduin south of Aerthir","Rumours abound of the strange Corsair, Jajax, who aided the Men of Linhir in crippling the Heirs of Castamir.","Aerthir can be found due south of Ost Anglebed along the shores of the Anduin.\
\
You have not found Jajax near Hata Kebir, but you should continue your search along the coast to the south of Aerthir.","Nimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.\
\
You found Jajax and Daxamat preparing to sail from Lebennin. You should tell Nimithil of your journey.","You discover Jajax and Daxamat preparing a boat!","'Ha! I had a feeling I couldn't sail away before you tracked me down one last time.\
\
'Or maybe I was waiting for you... who can tell?\
\
'Dax and I were just about to set sail, but would you do me the honour of sharing one of these fine bottles of wine with us?'","Jajax can be found along the coastline to the south of Aerthir.\
\
You have shared wine with Jajax and should speak to him once more.","'Ever since your return from Hata Kebir with the brothers of Linhir, rumours have cropped up throughout Lebennin about the one they called Jajax.\
\
'It is said that he himself set fire to the Corsair fleet on the shores, cut an ear from one of the Heirs, and then vanished along with his brother into the trees of Lebennin.\
\
'Where now has he gone? Does he still remain in our lands, or does he sail on towards future heroics?\
\
'Search near the camp on the shore for him, and then search the coast if you do not find him. I wonder where his plans shall take him next....'","A bottle of wine can be found in the basket next to Jajax.\
\
Jajax has asked you to share a bottle of fine wine with him and Daxamat.","Epilogue: Sailing Into The Dawn","Talk to Jajax","Hata Kebir can be found far to the south-east of Ost Anglebed.\
\
Nimithil has asked you to seek out Jajax, if he still remains in Lebennin. You should begin your search near Hata Kebir.","Return to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed","'What a peculiar man that Jajax is, ${PLAYER}. I doubt we shall ever know a Corsair like him again.\
\
'You have shown us all that one day there might be peace between our peoples, and that some friendships run deeper than blood.'","You have found no sign of the two brothers, and should search further west along the shore","'The Scourge certainly kept the best stock for himself... ah well, he won't be needin' it anymore.\
\
'Listen here, ${PLAYER}. Dax and I need to go now. I don't know where we're heading, but it certainly isn't here.\
\
'I've had enough of Gondor... I miss my home in Umbar, and besides, there are plenty of other places for me to sail.\
\
'I shall always remember the times we had, and I shall try to remember the drinks we shared. I suppose this is where our paths split, my adventurous friend.'","Share a drink with Jajax and Daxamat"},
[4816]={"Talk to the shade of Tárandil by the waggon in Laerlad","The shade of Tárandil is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Tárandil, and says nothing.","'My dagger cut deeply, and I perished. But although the line of my life had reached its end, I was to have no rest. The oath I swore was to a power far greater and darker than that sworn by Rioc, and it bound me to these cursed fields long past the night my blood was spilt. I searched in vain for Sauron's Ring, but my prize was lost, and with it all my hopes.\
\
'I yielded to my misery, and rage consumed me. So great was my ire that all fled before me, and as the centuries passed I left behind all memory of my life. All I knew was anger and resentment, and I gave the death that was denied me to all who entered my domain. Orc, Elf, or Man... no creature was safe from my wrath.\
\
'But then, amid the confused tatters of my memory, one crossed my path who I knew of old. He wore the appearance of an old pilgrim, cloaked in grey, but I knew this vagabond's form hid a greater power. How could he have returned? I confronted him, and my spirit was seared by the heat of the power he kept hidden. Then I was afraid, and fled; but he followed close behind, and cast a spell most cruel. I was banished, but the force of my oath prevented my leaving; in distress, my very being was torn asunder, and I knew no more for long years.\
\
'But something changed, something far away and yet ever-present, and my form coalesced in agony out of the mist. The pain I felt in that moment was worse than every torment I ever experienced, save one: the anguish of losing Bravantel and Héol forevermore. That pain I feel still, and it will never abate.'","Talk to the shade of Tárandil and complete 'Instance: The Disaster'","Epilogue: The Disaster","The shade of Tárandil has manifested for a single purpose: he wishes to make his confession.","'Speak on, shade. You have brought us this far along your sorrowful recollection, and should not leave us here.'","'Tárandil's confession draws to its close, ${PLAYER}. We must hear what he has to say, though the ending is known to us.'","'As my foster-father's company followed the northward road between marsh and forest, I saw the signs of Gurnákh's raiding-party everywhere. Each snapping twig, every bird taken flight, all seemed to herald the missteps of the Orcs. \\qThe maps are changed,\\q I remember thinking as the company neared my scouted location. \\qThe course of the river is different than it was when we came south, and the lay of the land may not be as I remembered. It is not going to work.\\q\
\
'Then there was no time left for doubt. If Adûnzagar could have repented of his treachery and stayed Tárandil, that time was gone when the Orcs attacked. I did not notice its passing, for at first the plan I had given the Orcs seemed without flaw. At first.\
\
'The darkness shielded their numbers, and enlarged the attacking force in the minds of Isildur's men. Still, they were valiant, and tempered by their travails during the war they had so recently fought. When there came an opening, my foster-father commanded they press further north.\
\
'But it was not the harbinger of victory it seemed, and the Orcs returned for the second of the attacks I had suggested.'"},
[4817]={"'Each member of the Ghad Imghêda is impressive. Until they learn I am not, I will stand beside them and do the best I can!'","'The people of the city loved my husband. I will rule as part of the Ghad Imghêda in his memory, and on their behalf.'","Jínen was on her way to the Gate of Songs north of the city.","Talk to the leadership of Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha","Talk to Jajax at Dâr Rapha","'The people called for me to join the Ghad Imghêda; as harbour-warden I could not refuse. I sought not to elevate my position, but with so many of the Heirsworn gone from the city, it would seem my days must be less eventful. This will fill them up.\
\
'To the Umbari who called for me to join this august body, I made this pledge: to remain vigilant, not only of our enemies but also of our friends, and our chosen leaders. It appears to this old sailor that much of the trouble began when Tumúldo sailed to Gondor, and that done at Azagath's command. The old Kindred should have sniffed out the Sea-shadow's evil before he could use it to deprive the city of such a hero as Tumúldo, who might have opposed him.\
\
'Others might be deceived, but not I, and not now the Ghad Imghêda!'","Rothog smiles at you, and his grin seems more ferocious than ever.","'Yes, I fought against the Heirsworn during the uprising; I am not afraid to speak of it.\
\
'They have always been the weakened side of the ship's hull, still long at sea, and I am not surprised that it eventually burst! The passage by the city of the Ordâkhai ships was a hammer-blow to that imperfection, and the Heirsworn believed their time had come at last to fully seize control once again. What made them so bold? I cannot say for certain, but whispers tell that many of their number had been secretly leaving the city for a number of weeks, rallied somewhere by the son of Balakhôr himself.\
\
'The uprising was short but effective, and a new Kindred has been formed to lead Umbar Baharbêl in the days to come: the Ghad Imghêda! They assemble even now at Dâr Rapha, up the hill to the east. That is where I am going, for I wish to get a look at them. On these wise counsellors we put our hopes!'","Talk to the leadership of the Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha","'One thing followed another, ${PLAYER}. I am not sure what happened. But I am glad to see you safe and alive!\
\
'At first I was just trying to carry out your will, telling the people what you told me... but as more and more folk learned that Hármelak and Khôltekh had imprisoned you and my brother, they became angrier and angrier. You helped many Umbari and Temámir alike when you came to these shores, ${PLAYER}, and it seems you have made more friends than you know!\
\
'What began in confusion became a rebellion, Ilma-ghôli, the rising tide, and then there was no stopping it! Try as I might, I could not convince those who flocked to us that I was not cut out to lead them... and now they have made me part of the Ghad Imghêda. I don't understand how this happened, and yet every step of the way has led me to this moment.\
\
'Is this how you feel every day, ${PLAYER}? I cannot get used to this!'","'I wear these burns proudly in memory of Belondor, ${PLAYER}. I believe he sails now in the company of his friend Sirgon, and they are not bound by the oceans of the world.\
\
'I sought not to join the Ghad Imghêda, but the people of the city demanded it. I could not refuse them. They ask for strength, and I possess it. It would be impolite to abandon them.'\
\
Rothog grins, a frightful sight.\
\
'Besides,' he says, 'all of my things are here.'","'Our return voyage was not as eventful as the first that brought you to these shores, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Umbar Baharbêl seemed on the very precipice of the cliff's edge when we departed, but all is now as it was. Let us ask some of the people nearby what transpired while we were away.\
\
'You go to the east and find someone willing to talk near the Northern Ship-yard. The workers there are always willing to spend the day in idle chatter, and the tidings we seek are the furthest thing from trivial!'","Some familiar faces await you: the Ghad Imghêda of Umbar Baharbêl","Someone at the Northern Ship-yard around the corner to the east may have further information for you concerning the political situation in Umbar Baharbêl.","'The Temámir and the Umbari people must work together, and not at cross-purposes. For that reason, I was chosen to join the Ghad Imghêda.\
\
'I feel I must apologize for the actions taken by Khôltekh during the past few weeks, ${PLAYER}. I have explained to the Umbari and to my own people that I consider it a failing of my own that I did not determine his true allegiances in time to prevent the tragedies that befell the city. I need not tell you that he acted alone and for his own interests, and it was not with the authority of the Shoreward Stone that he fell in with Ordâkh or with the Orcs of Mordor that were seen upon one of the vessels as it passed the city. I am grateful for the assemblage of Temámir who came to Thargushakâl and informed me of his treachery during the early hours of the uprising. They will be rewarded!\
\
'The actions of Khôltekh shame his people. The Umbari can rest more easily now that I have joined the Ghad Imghêda.'","'My brother Dax stands with this new Kindred as if he were one of them! That is an oversight, surely?'","Your return to Umbar Baharbêl has revealed a change in the political situation of the city.","'Despite the land where he was born, my husband was a man of Umbar. The wife of such a man must be prepared for the voyage on which he might not return, and I was.'\
\
Mêshka smiles sadly.\
\
'That makes it little easier, ${PLAYER}, but one thing has lightened my sorrow. The people of the city loved my husband, and they grieve with me. The burden is shared across every Ward of Umbar Baharbêl, and so made less.\
\
'They asked me to join the Ghad Imghêda and to rule in Belondor's stead. I agreed, and so honour my husband's memory and the love he held for this city and its people.'","Talk to Jínen outside the Gate of Songs","Dâr Rapha is up the hill to the east of the Gate of Songs, outside the city.","'The actions of Khôltekh shame his people and his city. The Umbari can rest more easily now that I have joined the Ghad Imghêda.'","Jajax has come to Dâr Rapha, outside the city.","'Someone will tell us what transpired while we were away. Umbar Baharbêl seemed on the very precipice of the cliff's edge when we departed, but all is now as it was! Find someone at the Northern Ship-yard. east of here, who is willing to talk.'","Epilogue: The Ghad Imghêda","'The Ghad Imghêda meets even now at Dâr Rapha, east of the city. That is where I am going, for I wish to get a look at them. On these wise counsellors we put our hopes!'","'One mystery remains to be solved.'","'How might things have transpired if Dax was locked away, and I was left to manage the uprising? Now that would result in a truly impressive Ghad Imghêda!'","'How could you not have heard? The Kindred of the Coins was overthrown, and a new Kindred raised in its place: the Ghad Imghêda, the Kindred Redeemed!\
\
'Hármelak Golden-hand and Khôltekh the Temámir were in league with Ordâkh, allying even with Orcs of Mordor! They thought to sell this city to its oppressors, but they counted not on us: the common men and women of Umbar, the ship-builders and the sailors, the merchants and the scholars, the fishermen and the labourers.\
\
'The people of Umbar Baharbêl rose up against them, and with one voice we spoke to them: \\qIt will not be so!\\q we shouted. The uprising lasted for the better part of the day, and into the night. There was bloodshed, for not every soldier at Hármelak's command threw down his weapons, but many saw the rightness of our cause and joined the just throng.\
\
'Another group opposed us during the uprising: the Heirsworn, who have long troubled the peace of the harbour. One of my workers fought against them on the night of the uprising, and can tell you more. Her name is Jínen, and she was on her way to the Gate of Songs north of the city just moments ago. If you hurry you may find her there.\
\
'But that is in the past. May the new Kindred better serve the interests of the Umbari people, free of the influences of Ordâkh!'","The leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.","Meet the Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha, up the hill to the east","Find someone at the Northern Ship-yard who will tell you the situation in the city","'The Heirsworn will no longer pose a threat to us. I will see to that.'","'May the new Kindred better serve the interests of the Umbari people, free of the influences of Ordâkh!'"},
[4818]={"Vágari has manifested for a single purpose: he wishes to make his confession.","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Tárandil, and says nothing.","Epilogue: The Wanderer's Confession","'Speak to Vágari, and we will judge him by the content of his confession.'","The shade of Isildur stares impassively at Vágari, and says nothing.","Vágari the Wanderer is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","Talk to Vágari and complete 'Instance: The Wanderer's Confession'","'The pieces fall into place, and I begin to see the sad road that brought the shade of Tárandil to this place, and this state. Could he have turned away from this course, and prevented the evil he would cause? For I guess at the ending, and it is sorrowful. Still we must hear it.'","Talk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad","Gandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.","'Let us hear what Vágari has to say.'","'My story begins long ago... so very long ago...'"},
[4819]={"Epilogue: The Waters of the Gilrain","You have discovered Garvir - alive and resting on the banks of the Gilrain!","DNT -- will not be seen","Search the banks of the Gilrain for a man","Amid a brief peace in Linhir, Erchar has become fascinated by the stories you have shared of the Maiden of the Gilrain.","'You do know him, then?\
\
'Indeed, these are very peculiar times....\
\
'I shall rouse him from his sleep, and carry him safely back to his brothers. He is fortunate to have one as caring as you in his life, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Return to them, and tell them of what has happened.'","'He... he is alive?\
\
'I cannot believe it, I...'\
\
Erchar is overcome with emotion, and begins weeping.\
\
'Herion, our brother lives yet!'","Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have learned that Garvir was saved by the Maiden of the Gilrain as he fell into the river. You should tell Erchar that his brother lives!","The man Roamingstar pulled from the Gilrain can be found along the nearby banks.\
\
Roamingstar rescued a man from the waters of the Gilrain and healed his wounds. You should examine the sleeping man.","Tell Erchar of Garvir's return","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it is good to see you once more....\
\
'You come bringing the thanks of a man of Dor-en-Ernil? It is most appreciated, though strange for one not of Lebennin.\
\
'Since you left to return to the cities of Man, a very curious thing has happened. You see, a wounded, honourable man was cast into my waters and left to die. I pulled him from the river and healed his wounds, but he has slept here ever since.\
\
'He has been through a great deal and still requires more rest, but perhaps you know who he is?\
\
'He is resting along the banks nearby....'","'My brothers, how I have missed you....\
\
'All went dark when I fell into the Gilrain, but then I awoke under the trees... and all my wounds and pain had gone!'\
\
Garvir rushes towards Herion and Erchar, embracing them.\
\
'And thank you, ${PLAYER}, for reuniting me with my brothers. There is no greater gift you could have given me, my dear friend.'","Talk to Roamingstar","Seek out Roamingstar in her glade","Garvir can be found in Linhir.\
\
Garvir has returned to Linhir, much to his brothers' amazement. You should speak to him, and welcome him home.","Talk to Garvir","'The days have been long since Garvir's passing, but I comfort myself in knowing that his sacrifice and the deeds of the river-maiden have saved so many lives.\
\
'Garvir is gone and I cannot change that, but the Maiden of the Gilrain still dwells in these lands. Tancestel's ramblings have made me wary of seeking her myself, but she knows well of you and would listen to your words.\
\
'If you would travel to her glade and offer her my truest thanks, I shall be most grateful.'","Before you can finish telling Erchar, Garvir walks into Linhir, smiling widely","Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Erchar wishes to thank the Maiden of the Gilrain for watching over the people of Central Gondor.","Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have discovered Garvir sleeping along the river-banks, much to your surprise. You should again speak to Roamingstar."},
[4820]={"Habla con Aran Verduno","Deberías volver a Puente de Caballetes o al Embarcadero de los Comerciantes","Vuelve a Embarcadero de los Comerciantes","'Ahora que la Liga del Hacha ha consolidado nuestra presencia en el Bosque Salvaje y ha enriquecido la vida de cada uno de nosotros, creo que es hora de hablar con la Hermandad de los Leñadores sobre la propiedad del Bosque Salvaje. Convoquemos una reunión entre nuestros grupos en terreno neutral dentro del Bosque Salvaje. Espero que allí podamos encontrar una solución al hecho de que nuestras dos facciones compitan por los mismos recursos.'","'Ahora que la Hermandad de los Leñadores ha consolidado su presencia en el Bosque Salvaje y ha logrado grandes avances, creo que es hora de hablar con la Liga del Hacha sobre la propiedad del Bosque Salvaje. Convoquemos una reunión entre nuestros grupos en terreno neutral dentro del Bosque Salvaje. Espero que allí podamos encontrar una solución pacífica para nuestras dos facciones, que compiten por los mismos recursos.'","Habla con Enid Picortiga","Vuelve a Puente de Caballetes","Ve al punto de encuentro entre Aran Verduno y Enid Picortiga","'Enid, la Liga del Hacha es más que bienvenida en Puente de Caballetes. Estableceremos un puesto comercial permanente en la ciudad para vosotros. Entonces está decidido: ya que ahora compartimos los mismos objetivos, unamos nuestros conocimientos y recursos y velemos juntos por el Bosque Salvaje. Tu propuesta es acertada. ¡De ahora en adelante nos conoceremos como la Liga del Bosque Salvaje!\
\
'${PLAYER}, Enid y los miembros de la Liga son buena gente. Si no estuviéramos tan ocupados con nuestros propios problemas y dificultades en el Bosque Salvaje, quizá nos hubiéramos unido antes en nuestras causas. Supongo que es una lección aprendida. Me alegro de que hayamos encontrado un terreno común en este día. El futuro del Bosque Salvaje es, sin duda, prometedor.'","Los dos líderes están en plena conversación cuando llegas","Los líderes de la Liga del Hacha y de la Hermandad de los Leñadores pretenden colaborar para alcanzar sus objetivos en el Bosque Salvaje.","Enid Picortiga se encuentra en el punto de encuentro en el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Enid Picortiga.","Encontrarás a Aran Verduno en el punto de encuentro del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Aran Verduno.","'Sí, Aran, creo que podemos colaborar para recolectar y preservar los recursos del bosque. La perdurabilidad del Bosque Salvaje es importante para la Liga del Hacha. ¿Será bienvenida la Liga del Hacha para comerciar y vender mercancías en Puente de Caballetes? Además, ¿qué opinas de mi propuesta sobre nuestras dos facciones?'","Epílogo: El Bosque Salvaje de las Tierras de Bree","Aran Verdduno y Enid Picortiga tienen previsto reunirse en el centro del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Debes dirigirte al punto de encuentro indicado."},
[4821]={"Find Draigoch's bones","The Weeping Warrior's thirst for dragon bones is almost an obsession","Find Thorog's bones with Sigrun's aid","Karazgar the Weeping Warrior may have eluded your grasp, but retracing his path has taught you something of value: seeking to counteract his own decline, he turned to the dragon-venom that both strengthened and poisoned him for so long. He suffers in undeath, bound to the dragon-kind that he despises and upon which he now relies.","The dwarf Sigrun can aid you in the Misty Mountains, as can Fotri in Forochel. Draigoch's Lair can be found in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith.\
\
You should seek the bones of the dragons Bregmor, Draigoch, and Thorog.","Learned more about Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior.","Epilogue: Trail of Rust","The cavern has clearly been disturbed, and snow-covered rust trails across the mountain","Completado","Find Bregmor's bones with Fotri's aid","Fróthi suggests seeking out other dead dragons for clues to the riddle of the Weeping Warrior's motives.","'Now, say you were to follow the path, where might it lead? Let me think. Hm... yes. If dragon bones are what this Weeping Warrior cares about, the Dale-lands are not the only place such things may be found. Can you think of any others? You are the worldly traveller, after all!'\
\
You mention Bregmor of Forochel, Draigoch of Enedwaith, and Thorog of the Misty Mountains.\
\
'You name familiar and unfamiliar worms, ${PLAYER}. I was not mistaken in thinking you worldly-wise! In this much I can guide you: seek Sigrun in the Misty Mountains and Fotri in Forochel. They are dwarves worthy of their beards and will be of great help to you. For Enedwaith, I am afraid, you are on your own.\
\
'Good luck, my friend!'"},
[4822]={"'Are you ready? I do not know what we will learn from Vóin's secret writing, but whatever it may be we will discover it together.\
\
'It is time to hear the rest of Vóin's tale.'","Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús and complete 'Instance: Vóin's Tale'","You have given Gandalf the glass shard you found locked in Khîl's home, and the Wizard believes it may prove crucial to revealing the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor.","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús.","Epilogue: Vóin's Tale","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, eager to decipher the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor.","'There is a moving radiance held within this glass, ${PLAYER}, and it reminds me of something: the rotating beacon atop Barad Cúron, Tower of the Crescent Moon, in Minas Morgul. Is this a shard of glass from the beacon in the tower's topmost chamber?\
\
'You have seen moon-letters before, and so have I. Can it be that Vóin wrote these secret words in the light of that beacon, knowing they could only be revealed by the same light? But what did he seek to hide? Did he record the location of the weapon sought by Gothmog?\
\
'We must read the secret writing in the Black Book, ${PLAYER}. Let me know if you are ready to do so.'","'Much that was obscured from us now seems clear, my friend. When the sword Dúnachar pierced Mordirith's form in the throne room of Carn Dûm, the purpose of the Witch-king was fulfilled, a thousand years later, but not in the manner for which he planned. Bonds were made that day, and months later, on the Pelennor Fields before Minas Tirith, they would be broken. He could not remember it, but one thousand years later, Eärnur's final act of resistance freed him from the domination of Mordor.'\
\
Gandalf closes the Black Book and looks up at you.\
\
'That is enough for now, my friend. We have come to the end of the moon-writing, but the discovery has stirred in me the certainty that I missed something in my earlier perusal of this tome. I do not know what it may have been, but I can sense its presence still.\
\
'Ah, mysteries upon mysteries. Perhaps I will return to this matter when we have satisfied our other charge. Yes, I fear we have spent too many hours in study and neglected our other tasks.'"},
[4824]={"Tarjeta de búsqueda completada.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Acaricia</rgb> a Garra, el perro del granjero Maggot","Reúne recuerdos en Bolsón Cerrado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Relatos de Eriador: Año Uno — Frodo","<rgb=#FF00FF>Acaricia</rgb> a Colmillo, el perro del granjero Maggot","'¿Lo puedes creer? ¡Dejaron los platos sucios! Bueno, ¡mejor así, digo yo!'","<rgb=#FF00FF>Desmáyate</rgb> en el campamento de los Montaraces bajo la Cima de los Vientos","Recuerdas aventuras del pasado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Y aun mientras se desvanecía, alcanzó a ver a Trancos saltar con una antorcha encendida...","Esta tarjeta de búsqueda contiene una lista de cosas por encontrar. ¡Podrían estar en cualquier lugar!","Cada primavera se celebra la Búsqueda del Tesoro del Aniversario para conmemorar una ocasión muy especial.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Esta versión de la misión incluye únicamente los objetivos que se encuentran en Eriador y está disponible para jugadores de todos los niveles.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Disfruta de una comida en la casa de Tom Bombadil","¡Completaste una tarjeta de búsqueda!","Has conversado con Lobelia","Las tarjetas cuelgan del Árbol de la Fiesta. Cada una contiene una búsqueda que puedes completar a tu propio ritmo.","La comida es abundante y reconfortante, y la bebida es agua clara y fría.","Habla con Frodo en la habitación de Bilbo en Rivendel","Saltó por los aires, rodó fuera de la mesa y luego ¡simplemente desapareció!","<rgb=#FF00FF>Baila</rgb> sobre una mesa en el Poney Pisador","Acaricias a Colmillo. ¡Buen chico!","Habla con Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón","Completado","'¡Qué alegría tener al viejo Gandalf, a Trancos y a mis viejos amigos conmigo cuando partamos! Aunque me pregunto hasta dónde llegaremos juntos y en qué punto nuestros caminos se separarán... si es que llegan a separarse.'","Acaricias a Garra. ¡Buen perro!"},
